<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed Yusuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1878</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed Yusuf was sultan of the Geledi in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-mahamud-ibrahim">Yusuf Mahamud Ibrahim</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobroon-dynasty">Gobroon dynasty</a>. He ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afgooye">Afgooye</a> over the lower Shabelle valley and its plantations, and dealt with the Sultanate of Zanzibar on the coast. He was killed fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bimaal">Bimaal</a> clan in 1878, after which the Geledi sultanate declined.</p></div>
